  "id": "brown-sequards-syndrome",
  "term": "Brown-Séquard’s syndrome",
  "definition": "Brown-Séquard’s syndrome is a neurological syndrome caused by damage to one side of the spinal cord. Below the injury, it typically involves weakness or paralysis and loss of position sense on the same side as the lesion, with loss of pain and temperature sensation on the opposite side, while touch is often preserved.",
